ion Opening Date 09/25/2025 Closing Date Continuous Bargaining Unit APSCUF Classification Temporary Description Benefits Job Summary Kutztown University of Pennsylvania enrolls approximately 7,500 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs. Located in a charming rural setting in Kutztown, Pennsylvania, the University is just a 20-minute drive from the metropolitan areas of Allentown/Bethlehem and Reading, and about an hour from the Philadelphia metropolitan area. The University seeks to hire employees with experience working with diverse populations. The Department of Secondary Education at Kutztown University invites applicants for our temporary adjunct pool in teacher education for the following areas: coursework in Principles of Teaching and Learning for secondary teacher candidates; supervision of student teaching, undergraduate and graduate coursework for the English as a Second Language (ESL) program; graduate courses for our Curriculum and Instruction MEd program; and graduate courses for our Principal and Supervisory Certificate programs. Undergraduate course offerings could be day or evening. Graduate courses are typically offered online. We are seeking colleagues who have a passion for preparing the next generation of teachers. In accordance with the Collective Bargaining Agreement, performance review and evaluation of faculty is based on effective teaching and fulfillment of professional responsibilities; continuing scholarly growth and professional development; and service. Minimum Qualifications Required qualifications: a Master's degree in the field of education, at least 5 years' experience teaching in PK-12. Preferred Qualifications Preferred: Doctorate; and at least one year of college-level teaching experience or equivalent; experience working with diverse learners; 7-12 certification(s); ESL Endorsement; Principal Certification. Applicants who meet the minimum requirements will be certified to be placed in our part-time adjunct faculty pool and will remain in the pool while the pool is active. As need arises, applicants in the pool will be considered and contacted for an on-campus interview. During the on-campus interview, successful interview and demonstration of abilities are required to be selected. Supplemental Information As part of the application, candidates must upload the following material to NeoEd: a letter of application, current curriculum vitae, copies of undergraduate and graduate transcripts (official transcripts must be supplied by the time of the virtual interview), and contact information for three professional references addressed to: Dr. Brenda Muzeta, Coordinator & Adjunct Pool Search Committee Chair, Only complete applications will be considered (all previously listed documents have been received). Successful interviews, reference checks, background clearances (PA Criminal, Child Abuse Clearance & FBI Clearance), and demonstration of ability are requisite qualifications for all positions. The University is very interested in hiring employees who have had extensive experience with diverse populations. Non-Discrimination Statement Kutztown University does not discriminate in employment or educational opportunities on the basis of sex, race, ethnicity, national origin, age, disability, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, or veteran status. To discuss a complaint of discrimination, please contact the Office of Social Equity, Old Main A-Wing, Room 02, by phone at 610-683-4700 or by e-mail at pena@kutztown.edu . Pursuant to Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Kutztown University does not discriminate on the basis of sex and prohibits sex discrimination in any education program or activity that it operates, including admissions and employment. Any inquiries regarding the application of Title IX at Kutztown University may be made to Bradley Davis, the University’s Title IX Coordinator, located in Old Main A-Wing, Room 02A, by phone at 610-683-4782 or by email 